{"id":"mahabharata-1-190","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":190,"title":"नवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 190 · The wedding of Draupadi","summary":{"en":"Drupada accepts. On successive days, with Dhaumya officiating, Draupadi marries each of the five brothers in turn, regaining her maidenhood each day by Vyasa's word, and Drupada gives them rich gifts.","kn":"ದ್ರುಪದನು ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧೌಮ್ಯರ ಪೌರೋಹಿತ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಕ್ರಮವಾಗಿ ದಿನದಿನವೂ ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಐವರು ಸಹೋದರರನ್ನು ವಿವಾಹವಾಗುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ವ್ಯಾಸರ ವಚನದಂತೆ ಪ್ರತಿದಿನ ಕನ್ಯಾತ್ವವನ್ನು ಮರಳಿ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತಾಳೆ; ದ್ರುಪದನು ಸಮೃದ್ಧ ಉಡುಗೊರೆಗಳನ್ನು ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"द्रुपद मान जाते हैं। धौम्य के पौरोहित्य में क्रमशः दिन-प्रतिदिन द्रौपदी पाँचों भाइयों से विवाह करती हैं, व्यास के वचन से हर दिन कौमार्य पुनः पाती हैं, और द्रुपद उन्हें प्रचुर उपहार देते हैं।","te":"ద్రుపదుడు అంగీకరిస్తాడు. ధౌమ్యుని పౌరోహిత్యంలో వరుసగా రోజుకొకరిని ద్రౌపది ఐదుగురు సోదరులను వివాహమాడుతుంది, వ్యాసుని వచనంతో ప్రతిరోజూ కన్యాత్వాన్ని తిరిగి పొందుతుంది; ద్రుపదుడు విరివిగా కానుకలిస్తాడు.","ta":"த்ருபதன் இசைகிறான். தௌம்யர் நடத்த, நாளுக்கு ஒருவராகத் திரௌபதி ஐந்து சகோதரர்களையும் மணக்கிறாள்; வியாஸரின் வாக்கால் ஒவ்வொரு நாளும் கன்னித்தன்மையை மீண்டும் பெறுகிறாள்; த்ருபதன் வளமான பரிசுகள் தருகிறான்.","ml":"ദ്രുപദൻ സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു. തുടർച്ചയായ ദിവസങ്ങളിൽ, ധൗമ്യന്റെ പൗരോഹിത്യത്തിൽ, ദ്രൗപദി അഞ്ചു സഹോദരന്മാരെയും ഓരോരുത്തരായി വിവാഹം കഴിക്കുന്നു; വ്യാസന്റെ വാക്കിനാൽ ഓരോ ദിവസവും അവൾ കന്യകാത്വം വീണ്ടെടുക്കുന്നു. ദ്രുപദൻ അവർക്ക് സമൃദ്ധമായ സമ്മാനങ്ങൾ നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.190; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"वैवाहिकपर्व","titleEn":"Vaivahika Parva (The wedding)","verses":[{"text":"द्रुपद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drupada said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अश्रुत्वैवं वचनं ते महर्षे\nमया पूर्वं यतितं कार्यमेतत् ।\nन वै शक्यं विहितस्यापयातुं\nतदेवेदमुपपन्नं विधानम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great sage, even before hearing your words I had striven to bring about this matter. What has been ordained cannot be turned aside, and so this arrangement has come about."}},{"n":2,"text":"दिष्टस्य ग्रन्थिरनिवर्तनीयः\nस्वकर्मणा विहितं नेह किंचित् ।\nकृतं निमित्तं हि वरैकहेतो-\nस्तदेवेदमुपपन्नं बहूनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The knot of destiny cannot be undone; nothing here is ordained apart from one's own deeds. The cause was set for the sake of one boon, and this very thing has come about for many husbands."}},{"n":3,"text":"यथैव कृष्णोक्तवती पुरस्ता-\nन्नैकान्पतीन्मे भगवान्ददातु ।\nस चाप्येवं वरमित्यब्रवीत्तां\nदेवो हि वेद परमं यदत्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said earlier, 'Let the venerable god give me not one husband, but many.' And he told her, 'So be it,' for the god knows what is supreme in this."}},{"n":4,"text":"यदि वायं विहितः शंकरेण\nधर्मोऽधर्मो वा नात्र ममापराधः ।\nगृह्णन्त्विमे विधिवत्पाणिमस्या\nयथोपजोषं विहितैषां हि कृष्णा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether this was ordained by Shankara as dharma or adharma, the fault is not mine. Let these men take her hand according to rule, as they please, for Krishna has been ordained for them."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीद्भगवान्धर्मराज-\nमद्य पुण्याहमुत पाण्डवेय ।\nअद्य पौष्यं योगमुपैति चन्द्रमाः\nपाणिं कृष्णायास्त्वं गृहाणाद्य पूर्वम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the venerable Vyasa said to the Dharmaraja: Today is an auspicious day, Pandava. Today the moon is joining Pushya; take Krishna's hand first today."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततो राजा यज्ञसेनः सपुत्रो\nजन्यार्थ युक्तं बहु तत्तदग्र्यम् ।\nसमानयामास सुतां च कृष्णा-\nमाप्लाव्य रत्नैर्बहुभिर्विभूष्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yajnasena with his son brought together many excellent things fit for the wedding guests, and bathed his daughter Krishna and adorned her with many jewels."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः सर्वे सुहृदस्तत्र तस्य\nसमाजग्मुः सचिवा मन्त्रिणश्च ।\nद्रष्टुं विवाहं परमप्रतीता\nद्विजाश्च पौराश्च यथाप्रधानाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all his friends, ministers and counsellors came there, and Brahmins and townspeople, according to rank, greatly pleased, to see the wedding."}},{"n":8,"text":"तत्तस्य वेश्मार्थिजनोपशोभितं\nविकीर्णपद्मोत्पलभूषिताजिरम् ।\nमहार्हरत्नौघविचित्रमाबभौ\nदिवं यथा निर्मलतारकाचितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His house, graced by those who came seeking gifts, its courtyard adorned with scattered lotuses and lilies, shone, colourful with heaps of costly jewels, like a sky studded with clear stars."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततस्तु ते कौरवराजपुत्रा\nविभूषिताः कुण्डलिनो युवानः ।\nमहार्हवस्त्रा वरचन्दनोक्षिताः\nकृताभिषेकाः कृतमङ्गलक्रियाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those Kuru princes, young and adorned with earrings, in costly garments, anointed with excellent sandal, having bathed and performed auspicious rites,"}},{"n":10,"text":"पुरोहितेनाग्निसमानवर्चसा\nसहैव धौम्येन यथाविधि प्रभो ।\nक्रमेण सर्वे विविशुश्च तत्सदो\nमहर्षभा गोष्ठमिवाभिनन्दिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"together with their fire-bright priest Dhaumya, lord, entered that hall in order according to rule, like great bulls entering a cow-pen, pleasing to behold."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततः समाधाय स वेदपारगो\nजुहाव मन्त्रैर्ज्वलितं हुताशनम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं चाप्युपनीय मन्त्रवि-\nन्नियोजयामास सहैव कृष्णया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the one who knew the Veda by heart poured offerings into the blazing fire with mantras, and the mantra-knower brought Yudhishthira and joined him with Krishna."}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रदक्षिणं तौ प्रगृहीतपाणी\nसमानयामास स वेदपारगः ।\nततोऽभ्यनुज्ञाय तमाजिशोभिनं\nपुरोहितो राजगृहाद्विनिर्ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"With hands joined, he made the two walk around the fire keeping it to their right, that master of the Vedas. Then the priest, having dismissed that one who adorned the courtyard, left the royal house."}},{"n":13,"text":"क्रमेण चानेन नराधिपात्मजा\nवरस्त्रियास्ते जगृहुस्तदा करम् ।\nअहन्यहन्युत्तमरूपधारिणो\nमहारथाः कौरववंशवर्धनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this order, day after day, those sons of kings, the great chariot-warriors of excellent form who enhance the Kuru line, took the hand of that excellent woman."}},{"n":14,"text":"इदं च तत्राद्भुतरूपमुत्तमं\nजगाद विप्रर्षिरतीतमानुषम् ।\nमहानुभावा किल सा सुमध्यमा\nबभूव कन्यैव गते गतेऽहनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"And there the Brahmin sage told this wonderful, supreme and superhuman thing: that great and slender-waisted lady became a maiden again with each passing day."}},{"n":15,"text":"कृते विवाहे द्रुपदो धनं ददौ\nमहारथेभ्यो बहुरूपमुत्तमम् ।\nशतं रथानां वरहेमभूषिणां\nचतुर्युजां हेमखलीनमालिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the wedding was done, Drupada gave many excellent riches to the great chariot-warriors: a hundred chariots adorned with fine gold, each with four horses and golden bridles and garlands,"}},{"n":16,"text":"शतं गजानामभिपद्मिनां तथा\nशतं गिरीणामिव हेमशृङ्गिणाम् ।\nतथैव दासीशतमग्र्ययौवनं\nमहार्हवेषाभरणाम्बरस्रजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"a hundred elephants with lotus-marked trappings, like a hundred mountains with golden peaks, and a hundred maidservants in their prime, in costly dress, ornaments, cloths and garlands."}},{"n":17,"text":"पृथक्पृथक्चैव दशायुतान्वितं\nधनं ददौ सौमकिरग्निसाक्षिकम् ।\nतथैव वस्त्राणि च भूषणानि\nप्रभावयुक्तानि महाधनानि ॥","meaning":{"en":"To each separately the Somaka king gave wealth of ten thousand units, with fire as witness, and likewise clothes and splendid, very valuable ornaments."}},{"n":18,"text":"कृते विवाहे च ततः स्म पाण्डवाः\nप्रभूतरत्नामुपलभ्य तां श्रियम् ।\nविजह्रुरिन्द्रप्रतिमा महाबलाः\nपुरे तु पाञ्चालनृपस्य तस्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"After the wedding the mighty Pandavas, like Indra in appearance, having gained that abundant prosperity rich in jewels, lived at their ease in the city of the Panchala king."}}]}]}